mapping "G401E.1" source="G401E" target="230381009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source G401E = Partiell epilepsi, enkel, utan medvetanstörning med sekundär generalisering =
        simple partial epilepsy with secondary generalization. No SNOMED CT concept captures this exact
        combination of focal-onset-with-secondary-generalization at the simple-partial level. Best
        available standard target is SNOMED CT 374915 (230381009), the Athena crosswalk target for ICD-10
        G40.1; it legitimately subsumes the source. Moderate tier because the secondary-generalization
        qualifier is lost.
        """
}
mapping "G401X.1" source="G401X" target="230381009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source G401X = Partiell epilepsi, enkel, utan medvetandestörning, ospecificerad = simple partial
        epilepsy, unspecified (residual of G40.1). SNOMED CT 374915 (230381009) is the Athena crosswalk
        target for ICD-10 G40.1 and subsumes the unspecified residual source. High tier because the
        crosswalk is verified and the parent is one level up.
        """
}
mapping "G402A.1" source="G402A" target="193000002" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source G402A SNOMED CT 193000002 = temporal lobe epilepsy, complex partial, with impairment of
        consciousness. Target SNOMED CT 4102345 (Disorder, std=S). The Swedish subcode is the lobe-specific
        complex-partial variant of G40.2; is the canonical standard concept for temporal lobe epilepsy
        (40636090 is its non-standard predecessor and itself maps to 4102345 via a Maps-to edge). Exact
        equivalence at the disorder level.
        """
}
mapping "G402B.1" source="G402B" target="230394006" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source G402B SNOMED CT 230394006 = frontal lobe epilepsy, complex partial, with impairment of
        consciousness. Target SNOMED CT 4047888 (Disorder, std=S). Exact equivalence at the disorder level;
        the Swedish subcode is the lobe-specific descendant of ICD-10 G40.2 whose parent maps to SNOMED CT
        Focal epilepsy.
        """
}
mapping "G402C.1" source="G402C" target="230403005" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source G402C SNOMED CT 230403005 = parietal lobe epilepsy, complex partial, with impairment of
        consciousness. Target SNOMED CT 4046206 (Disorder, std=S). Exact equivalence at the disorder level.
        """
}
mapping "G402D.1" source="G402D" target="230404004" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source G402D SNOMED CT 230404004 = occipital lobe epilepsy, complex partial, with impairment of
        consciousness. Target SNOMED CT 4046207 (Disorder, std=S). Exact equivalence at the disorder level.
        """
}
mapping "G402E.1" source="G402E" target="230381009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source G402E SNOMED CT 230381009 = complex partial epilepsy with secondary generalization. ICD-10
        base G40.2 maps to SNOMED CT 374915 (Focal epilepsy). The source bundles focal-onset
        complex-partial epilepsy PLUS secondary generalized seizures; no single standard SNOMED CT concept
        captures the full combination (4070660 is non-standard, U). Target 374915 (Focal epilepsy,
        std=S) is the broader focal-epilepsy ancestor that subsumes the focal aspect; the
        secondary-generalization component is uncovered. Recorded as broader for the focal axis; the
        missing generalization axis would warrant a separate partial target if a standard concept
        existed.
        """
}
mapping "G402F.1" source="G402F" target="230381009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source G402F SNOMED CT 230381009 = complex partial epilepsy with impairment of consciousness,
        psychomotor. is a legacy synonym for complex partial / focal-impaired-awareness epilepsy without
        lobe specification. ICD-10 G40.2 maps to SNOMED CT 374915 (Focal epilepsy, std=S). No single
        standard SNOMED CT concept encodes as a disorder; 374915 is the closest defensible broader
        ancestor. Moderate tier: legacy source terminology, parent-level crosswalk.
        """
}
mapping "G402X.1" source="G402X" target="230381009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source G402X SNOMED CT 230381009 = complex partial epilepsy with impairment of consciousness,
        unspecified. Unspecified subtype of ICD-10 G40.2, which maps to SNOMED CT 374915 (Focal epilepsy,
        std=S). With no lobe specified, the only defensible standard target is the focal-epilepsy
        parent. Moderate tier: unspecified source, parent-level crosswalk.
        """
}
